From: Notebook OS <benwhiting810@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wm: keep the DOCK panel (menu bar) above dialogs on screen

Matchbox stacks _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_DOCK panels *below* dialog windows
(see wm_activate_client() and dockbar_client_show()). Notebook OS uses a
single full-screen, shaped DOCK window as its system menu bar and draws
its dropdown menus inside that same window; the Finder and the desktop
widget column are floating DIALOGs. Because dialogs outrank the panel,
a dropdown opening over the Finder rendered *behind* it.

stack_sync_to_display() -> stack_get_window_list() is the single choke
point that projects matchbox's internal stack onto the X server via
XRestackWindows(). Emit panel frames first (topmost) there so the bar and
its in-window dropdowns always stack above dialogs, without disturbing the
internal stack/focus bookkeeping. A mapped fullscreen app (MBCLIENT_TYPE_APP
with _NET_WM_STATE_FULLSCREEN) still covers the panel, preserving the
"fullscreen app owns the screen" behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Notebook OS <benwhiting810@gmail.com>
---
 src/stack.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/stack.c b/src/stack.c
--- a/src/stack.c
+++ b/src/stack.c
@@ -185,6 +185,7 @@
   Window *win_list;
   Client *c;
   int     i = 0;
+  Bool    fullscreen_app = False;
 
   if (!w->stack_n_items) return NULL;
 
@@ -192,8 +193,28 @@
 
   dbg("%s() called, list is ", __func__);
 
+  /* Notebook OS: the panel (a DOCK) is the system menu bar and draws its
+   * dropdown menus inside its own full-screen shaped window. Matchbox stacks
+   * panels *below* dialogs, so a dropdown opening over the Finder (a floating
+   * dialog) is hidden behind it. Emit panel frames first (topmost) so the bar
+   * and its menus always stack above dialogs -- unless a fullscreen app owns
+   * the screen, in which case the panel keeps matchbox's default order so the
+   * app can cover it. */
+  stack_enumerate(w, c)
+    if (c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_APP && c->mapped
+	&& (c->flags & CLIENT_FULLSCREEN_FLAG))
+      fullscreen_app = True;
+
+  if (!fullscreen_app)
+    stack_enumerate_reverse(w, c)
+      if (c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_PANEL)
+	win_list[i++] = c->frame;
+
   stack_enumerate_reverse(w, c)
   {
+    if (!fullscreen_app && c->type == MBCLIENT_TYPE_PANEL)
+      continue;
+
     dbg("%i:%li, ", i, c->frame);
 
     win_list[i++] = c->frame;
